    Act 19: failure-count recovery, durable handoff queue, commit-age signal
    
    Implements the Office Continuity and Handoff Integrity Act (enacted 2026-10-19).
    
    §3.1 Failure-count-based session reset (government/office-recovery.sh):
    a durable per-office failure record with a reset decision decidable from the
    record (3 consecutive transient failures within 30 min, 1800 s cooldown), not
    from the transient agent state an oscillating agent defeats. A progress guard
    skips the reset when the office committed durable work since its last failure;
    permanent failures are surfaced, never silently reset. Wired into
    branch-bootstrap.sh, clerk-liveness.sh and seat-liveness.sh.
    
    §3.2 Durable handoff queue (government/handoff-queue.{sh,py}):
    records/handoffs/ is the executive dispatch's single input. executive-cycle.sh
    reads the queue FIRST; a read failure aborts the cycle (no generic dispatch),
    and any open handoff suppresses the generic eligible-issue prompt. Prompt text
    moved to government/prompts/ templates.
    
    §3.3 Per-office commit-age signal (government/commit-age.sh).
    
    Tests updated/added; full suite green.

